              = succeed "," do
                %em Moonshine for Rudvalis’s sporadic group I
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0609/0609449v2.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Vertex operator algebras over
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-archimedean+fields"} non-archimedean fields
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Kac"}> Victor Kac
              ,
              %em Non-Archimedean vertex algebras
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.09651"}> arXiv:2304.09651
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Classification of strongly rational holomorphic vertex operator algebras of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+charge"} central charge
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 24
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq 24
            (of relevance in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            and
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monstrous+moonshine"} monstrous moonshine
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adrian+Norbert+Schellekens"}> Adrian Norbert Schellekens
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Meromorphic
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo =
                          %mn 24
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = 24
                    Conformal Field Theories
                %strong 153
                (1993) 159-186 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02099044"}> doi:10.1007/BF02099044
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chongying+Dong"}> Chongying Dong
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geoffrey+Mason"} Geoffrey Mason
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Holomorphic vertex operator algebras of small central charges
                %strong 213
                2 (2004) 253–266 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0203005"}> arXiv:math/0203005
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/pjm.2004.213.253"} doi:10.2140/pjm.2004.213.253
            %li
              %p
                Philip Boyle Smith, Ying-Hsuan Lin, Yuji Tachikawa, Yunqin Zheng,
                %em
                  Classification of chiral fermionic CFTs of central charge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 16
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq 16
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16917"}> arXiv:2303.16917
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Brandon C. Rayhaun,
                %em Bosonic rational conformal field theories in small genera, chiral fermionization, and symmetry/subalgebra duality
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16921"}> arXiv:2303.16921
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerald+H%C3%B6hn"}> Gerald Höhn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sven+M%C3%B6ller"} Sven Möller
                %em Classification of self-dual vertex operator superalgebras of central charge at most 24
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.17190"}> arXiv:2303.17190
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p On equivalence of VOAs:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Sven Möller, Brandon C. Rayhaun:
                %em Equivalence Relations on Vertex Operator Algebras, I: Genus
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.07117"}> arXiv:2408.07117
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Sven Möller, Brandon C. Rayhaun:
                %em Equivalence Relations on Vertex Operator Algebras, II: Witt Equivalence and Orbifolds
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.18166"}> arXiv:2410.18166
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            of VOAs
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"}> Terry Gannon
              , Andrew Riesen:
              %em Orbifolds of Pointed Vertex Operator Algebras I
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.00809"}> arXiv:2410.00809
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#AsOperadAlgebras As algebras over the holomorphic sphere operad
          %p The original article with the interpretation of vertex operator algebras as holomorphic algebras over the holomorphic punctured sphere operad is
          %ul
            %li#Huang91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yi-Zhi+Huang"}> Yi-Zhi Huang
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric interpretation of vertex operator algebras
              %strong 88
              (1991) pp. 9964-9968 (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.88.22.9964"}> doi:10.1073/pnas.88.22.9964
              )
          %p A standard textbook summarizing these results is
          %ul
            %li#HuangCFT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yi-Zhi+Huang"}> Yi-Zhi Huang
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Two-dimensional conformal geometry and vertex operator algebras
              %a{:href => "http://books.google.hr/books?isbn=0817638296"} gbooks
          %p
            As mentioned in the
            %a{:href => "http://books.google.com/books?id=SUUdknTpYjEC&pg=PR11&lpg=PR11&dq=%22vertex+operator+algebras%22+%22trimble%22&source=bl&ots=v3GHx_ra2M&sig=TW5MzAtDi4n_gJjvUHb6eELoAXQ&hl=en&ei=9jdnSoXqKJiCtge6xqDuDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4"} acknowledgements
            there,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd Trimble
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
            had a hand in making the operadic picture manifest itself here.
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yi-Zhi+Huang"}> Yi-Zhi Huang
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Meromorphic open-string vertex algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 54
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.4806686"} doi:10.1063/1.4806686
          %p Other operadic approaches are known, e.g. an earlier one in:
          %ul
            %li
              Bojko Bakalov, Alessandro D’Andrea,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Kac"} Victor Kac
              = succeed "," do
                %em Theory of finite pseudoalgebras
              %strong 162
              (2001), no. 1, 1–140,
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2003c:17020"} MR2003c:17020
          %p
            and even earlier treatments via coloured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized multicategories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relaxed+multicategory"} relaxed multicategory
          %p
            Huang’s student
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liang+Kong"} Liang Kong
            developed these results further, generalizing them to open-closed CFTs and to non-chiral, i.e. completely general CFTs. See
          %ul
            %li#Kong08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liang+Kong"}> Liang Kong
              ,
              %em Open-closed field algebras
              Commun. Math. Physics. 280, 207-261 (2008),
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610293"} math.QA/0610293
          %h3#as_factorization_algebras As factorization algebras
          %p
            Discussion of vertex operator algebras as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebras+of+observables"} factorization algebras of observables
            is in section 6.3 and section 6.5 of
          %ul#Gwilliam
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"}> Owen Gwilliam
              ,
              %em Factorization algebras and free field theories
              PhD thesis (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~gwilliam/thesis.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %ul
            %li
              Emily Cliff,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universal factorization spaces and algebras
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.08122"} arxiv:1608.08122
          %blockquote
            %p We introduce categories of weak factorization algebras and factorization spaces, and prove that they are equivalent to the categories of ordinary factorization algebras and spaces, respectively. This allows us to define the pullback of a factorization algebra or space by an 'etale morphism of schemes, and hence to define the notion of a universal factorization space or algebra. This provides a generalization to higher dimensions and to non-linear settings of the notion of a vertex algebra.
          %h3#ReferencesAsCoalgebrasOverAComonad As coalgebras over a comonad
          %p
            On vertex operator algebras as
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebras+over+a+comonad"} coalgebras over a comonad
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jethro+van+Ekeren"}> Jethro van Ekeren
              ,
              %em A quantum field comonad
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.18223"}> arXiv:2305.18223
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#relation_to_modular_tensor_categories Relation to modular tensor categories
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+categories"} representation categories
            of (rational) vertex operator algebras (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+categories"}> modular tensor categories
            ) are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Huang
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yi-Zhi+Huang"}> Yi-Zhi Huang
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Vertex operator algebras, the Verlinde conjecture and modular tensor categories
                %strong 102
                (2005) 5352-5356
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0412261"} arXiv:math/0412261
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0409901102"} doi:10.1073/pnas.0409901102
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %li#GannonHoehn
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"}> Terry Gannon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerald+H%C3%B6hn"} Gerald Höhn
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ksu.edu/~gerald/voas/"} The online database of Vertex Operator Algebras and Modular Categories
          %h3#as_chiral_algebras As chiral algebras
          %p
            An algebrogeometric version is due Beilinson and Drinfel’d and called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+algebra"} chiral algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                E. Frenkel, N. Reshetikhin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards deformed chiral algebras
                %a{:href => "http://arXiv.org/abs/q-alg/9706023"} q-alg/9706023
            %li
              %p
                Ruthi Hortsch,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A universal approach to vertex algebras
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.0027"} arxiv/1006.0027
          %p Much algebraic insight to algebraic structures in CFT is in unfinished notes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Beilinson"}> A. Beilinson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B.+Feigin"} B. Feigin
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on conformal field theory
          %h3#relation_to_2d_conformal_field_theory Relation to 2d conformal field theory
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yi-Zhi+Huang"}> Yi-Zhi Huang
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two-dimensional conformal geometry and vertex operator algebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4612-4276-5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-4276-5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"}> Terry Gannon
                \:
                %em Exotic quantum subgroups and extensions of affine Lie algebra VOAs – part I
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.07287"}> arXiv:2301.07287
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yi-Zhi+Huang"}> Yi-Zhi Huang
              ,
              %em Representation theory of vertex operator algebras and orbifold conformal field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.01172"}> arXiv:2004.01172
              )
          %p
            Relation specifically to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+nets"} conformal nets
          %ul
            %li#CarpiKawahigahshiLongoWeiner15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastiano+Carpi"}> Sebastiano Carpi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yasuyuki+Kawahigashi"} Yasuyuki Kawahigashi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Longo"} Roberto Longo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From vertex operator algebras to conformal nets and back
                %strong 254
                1213 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/memo/1213"}> doi:10.1090/memo/1213
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1503.01260"} arXiv:1503.01260
            %li#Carpi16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastiano+Carpi"}> Sebastiano Carpi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Operator algebras and vertex operator algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1603.06742"} arXiv:1603.06742
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789813226609_0508"} doi:10.1142/9789813226609_0508
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+G.+Henriques"}> André G. Henriques
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+E.+Tener"} James E. Tener
                %em Every conformal net has an associated unitary VOA
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.20735"}> arXiv:2507.20735
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebras"} super vertex operator algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastiano+Carpi"}> Sebastiano Carpi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tiziano+Gaudio"} Tiziano Gaudio
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Hillier"} Robin Hillier
              %em From vertex operator superalgebras to graded-local conformal nets and back
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.14263"}> arXiv:2304.14263
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+E.+Tener"}> James E. Tener
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representation theory in chiral conformal field theory: from fields to observables
              %strong 25
              (2019) 76 [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00029-019-0526-3"}> doi:10.1007/s00029-019-0526-3
              ,
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.08168"} arXiv:1810.08168
          %p
            Relation of the corresponding
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ribbon+categories"} ribbon categories
          %ul
            %li#Gui18
              Bin Gui,
              %em Categorical extensions of conformal nets
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.04470"}> arXiv:1812.04470
              )
          %h3#deformations Deformations
          %p There is an interesting theory of deformation quantization of VOAs from
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"}> Pavel Etingof
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"} David Kazhdan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Lie bialgebras. V. Quantum vertex operator algebras
              %p
                Selecta Math. (N.S.) 6 (2000), no. 1, 105–130,
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2002i:17022"} MR2002i:17022
          %p Deformation quantization of chiral algebras are studied by
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Tamarkin"}> Dmitry Tamarkin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformations of chiral algebras
          %p
            A class of “free” vertex algebras are also quantized using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Batalin-Vilkovisky+formalism"} Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Si+Li"}> Si Li
              ,
              %em Vertex algebras and quantum master equation
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.01292"}> arxiv/1612.01292
              )
        .revisedby
